#: ../../../containers.rst:2
msgid "Container"
msgstr "容器"

#: ../../../containers.rst:4
msgid ""
"Xonsh publishes a handful of containers, primarily targeting CI and "
"automation use cases. All of them are published on `Docker Hub <https://hub."
"docker.com/u/xonsh>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:6
msgid "``xonsh/xonsh``: A base container providing basic xonsh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:7
msgid "``xonsh/xonsh-interactive``: xonsh with additions for people"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:8
msgid "``xonsh/xonsh-github-action``: xonsh with additions for GitHub Actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:10
msgid "All containers use the same tagging scheme:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:12
msgid "``<version>``/``latest``: Based on ``python:3`` (Debian Buster)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:13
msgid ""
"``<version>-slim``/``slim``: Based on ``python:3-slim`` (Debian Buster, slim "
"variant)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:14
msgid ""
"``<version>-alpine``/``alpine``: Based on ``python:3-alpine`` (Alpine Linux)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:16
msgid ""
"You can select specific versions of xonsh. However, you cannot select "
"specific versions of Python. Everything is rebuilt daily."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:18
msgid ""
"All containers include an ``xpip`` utility to let you easily install "
"packages from a Dockerfile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:20
msgid ""
"The container source can be found in the `container project <https://github."
"com/xonsh/container>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:23
msgid "``xonsh/xonsh``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:25
msgid "(`Docker Hub <https://hub.docker.com/r/xonsh/xonsh>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:27
msgid ""
"A basic container, including Python itself, xonsh, and the linux extras. "
"This container is deliberately kept minimal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:31
msgid "``xonsh/xonsh-interactive``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:33
msgid "(`Docker Hub <https://hub.docker.com/r/xonsh/xonsh-interactive>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:35
msgid ""
"A container made for humans (such as getting a shell inside of a pod). It "
"includes prompt toolkit and pygments so that xonsh is more usable "
"interactively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:39
msgid "``xonsh/xonsh-github-action``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:41
msgid "(`Docker Hub <https://hub.docker.com/r/xonsh/xonsh-github-action>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:43
msgid "A container with extras for GitHub Actions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:45
msgid "First, some of the inputs are parsed into more helpful forms:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:47
msgid ""
"``$GITHUB_EVENT``: The event that triggered the action (parsed from "
"``$GITHUB_EVENT_PATH``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:48
msgid ""
"``$INPUT``: The input arguments configured in the workflow (from "
"``$INPUT_*``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:50
msgid ""
"In addition, if you have `PyGithub <https://github.com/PyGithub/PyGithub>`_ "
"or `gqlmod <https://gqlmod.readthedocs.io/en/stable/>`_ installed, and an "
"authentication token was found, they will be configured:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:52
msgid "PyGithub: A ``Github`` object can be found at ``$GITHUB``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../containers.rst:53
msgid ""
"gqlmod: the token will be applied globally and the library will be ready to "
"use"
msgstr ""
